<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<title>Automation review: {{ business.display_name }}</title>
<style>
  @page {
    size: A4;
    margin: 14mm 14mm 16mm 14mm;
    @bottom-center {
      content: "Generated by an AI system on {{ generated_on }}. Rubric {{ rubric.version }}. Page " counter(page) " of " counter(pages);
      font-family: "DejaVu Sans", Arial, sans-serif;
      font-size: 7pt;
      color: #6b7785;
    }
  }
  * { box-sizing: border-box; }
  body {
    font-family: "DejaVu Sans", Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;
    font-size: 8.6pt;
    line-height: 1.34;
    color: #1c2530;
    margin: 0;
  }
  h1 { font-size: 15pt; margin: 0 0 1mm 0; letter-spacing: -0.2pt; }
  h2 { font-size: 9.4pt; margin: 4.5mm 0 1.6mm 0; text-transform: uppercase;
       letter-spacing: 0.5pt; color: #46586c; border-bottom: 0.5pt solid #ccd4dd;
       padding-bottom: 1mm; }
  p { margin: 0 0 1.6mm 0; }
  .subtitle { color: #5b6a7a; font-size: 8.4pt; margin-bottom: 3mm; }
  .notice {
    border: 0.6pt solid #b3762a;
    background: #fdf6ea;
    color: #5c3d0c;
    padding: 2mm 2.5mm;
    margin-bottom: 3mm;
    font-size: 7.8pt;
  }
  .notice ul { margin: 1mm 0 0 4mm; padding: 0; }
  .notice li { margin-bottom: 0.6mm; }
  table { width: 100%; border-collapse: collapse; margin-bottom: 2mm; }
  th {
    text-align: left; font-size: 7.4pt; text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.4pt; color: #55677a; border-bottom: 0.6pt solid #9aa8b8;
    padding: 1.2mm 1.6mm;
  }
  td { padding: 1.4mm 1.6mm; border-bottom: 0.4pt solid #e1e7ee; vertical-align: top; }
  td.num, th.num { text-align: right; white-space: nowrap; }
  .rank { color: #7a8899; width: 6mm; }
  .pname { font-weight: bold; }
  .pmeta { color: #6b7785; font-size: 7.4pt; }
  .band { white-space: nowrap; font-size: 7.6pt; padding: 0.5mm 1.4mm;
          border-radius: 1.4mm; border: 0.5pt solid; }
  .band-strong { color: #1c5b34; border-color: #1c5b34; background: #eaf5ee; }
  .band-pilot { color: #1e4f7a; border-color: #1e4f7a; background: #eaf1f8; }
  .band-watch { color: #7a5a17; border-color: #7a5a17; background: #fbf3e2; }
  .band-not_a_fit { color: #6b7785; border-color: #6b7785; background: #f2f4f7; }
  .score { font-weight: bold; }
  .capped { font-size: 7pt; color: #7a5a17; }
  .detail { border: 0.5pt solid #d5dce4; padding: 2.2mm 2.6mm; margin-bottom: 2mm; }
  .detail h3 { font-size: 9pt; margin: 0 0 1.4mm 0; }
  .crit { width: 100%; border-collapse: collapse; }
  .crit td { border: none; padding: 0.7mm 0; font-size: 7.8pt; }
  .crit td.label { width: 30mm; color: #46586c; }
  .crit td.val { width: 9mm; font-weight: bold; text-align: right; padding-right: 2mm; }
  .crit td.why { color: #34424f; }
  .disclosure {
    margin-top: 3.5mm; padding-top: 2mm; border-top: 0.5pt solid #ccd4dd;
    color: #55677a; font-size: 7.4pt;
  }
  .next { font-size: 7.9pt; }
  .next li { margin-bottom: 0.8mm; }
  ol.next { margin: 0 0 0 4.5mm; padding: 0; }
</style>
</head>
<body>

<h1>Automation review: {{ business.display_name }}</h1>
<p class="subtitle">
  {{ business.industry }} &middot; {{ business.headcount }} people &middot;
  {{ opportunities | length }} process{{ "es" if opportunities | length != 1 else "" }} reviewed
  {%- if intake.collected_on %} &middot; intake collected {{ intake.collected_on }}{% endif %}
</p>

{% if warnings %}
<div class="notice">
  <strong>Read this before the rankings.</strong>
  <ul>
    {% for warning in warnings %}
    <li>{{ warning }}</li>
    {% endfor %}
  </ul>
</div>
{% endif %}

<h2>Ranked opportunities</h2>
<table>
  <thead>
    <tr>
      <th class="rank">no.</th>
      <th>Process</th>
      <th>Recommendation</th>
      <th class="num">Score</th>
      <th>Main limit</th>
    </tr>
  </thead>
  <tbody>
    {% for item in summary_rows %}
    <tr>
      <td class="rank">{{ item.rank }}</td>
      <td>
        <span class="pname">{{ item.process.name }}</span><br>
        <span class="pmeta">{{ item.process.volume.describe() }} &middot;
          {{ item.process.people.count }} person{{ "s" if item.process.people.count != 1 else "" }} &middot;
          {{ item.process_map.step_count }} steps</span>
      </td>
      <td>
        <span class="band band-{{ item.band.id }}">{{ item.band.label }}</span>
        {% if item.was_capped %}<br><span class="capped">capped from {{ item.band_before_caps.label }}</span>{% endif %}
      </td>
      <td class="num score">{{ item.weighted_score | score }}</td>
      <td class="pmeta">{{ item.weakest.label }} ({{ item.weakest.raw_score }}/{{ rubric.scale_max }})</td>
    </tr>
    {% endfor %}
  </tbody>
</table>
{% if hidden_row_count %}
<p class="pmeta">{{ hidden_row_count }} further process{{ "es" if hidden_row_count != 1 else "" }}
  scored below these and are listed in the full markdown report.</p>
{% endif %}

{% if opportunities %}
{% set top = opportunities[0] %}
<h2>Highest ranked: {{ top.process.name }}</h2>
<div class="detail">
  <table class="crit">
    {% for criterion in top.criteria %}
    <tr>
      <td class="label">{{ criterion.label }}{% if criterion.inverted %} (inverted){% endif %}</td>
      <td class="val">{{ criterion.raw_score }}/{{ rubric.scale_max }}</td>
      <td class="why">{{ criterion.rationale }}</td>
    </tr>
    {% endfor %}
  </table>
</div>
<p class="next">
  Weighted score {{ top.weighted_score | score }} out of {{ rubric.scale_max }}.00, which places it in
  {{ top.band.label }}. The strongest part of the case is {{ top.strongest.label | lower }}. The part
  most likely to stop it is {{ top.weakest.label | lower }}.
  {% for cap in top.applied_caps %}
  The score alone would place this in {{ cap.band_before.label }}, and it is held at
  {{ cap.band_after.label }} because {{ cap.criterion_label | lower }} scored {{ cap.raw_score }}
  out of {{ rubric.scale_max }}. {{ cap.cap.reason }}
  {% endfor %}
</p>
{% endif %}

<h2>What to do with this</h2>
<ol class="next">
  <li>Check the figures. Volumes and time estimates came from the intake and were not verified.</li>
  <li>Read the process maps in the full report and correct any step the engine got wrong.</li>
  <li>Take the highest ranked item only, and time box a test of it before committing to anything.</li>
</ol>

<p class="disclosure">
  {{ disclosure }}
  Generated {{ generated_on }} against rubric {{ rubric.version }} by judge
  {{ result.judge_id }} in {{ result.judge_mode }} mode. This line repeats what the page
  footer says, because not every PDF renderer produces the footer.
</p>

</body>
</html>
